    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/977407?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Computational Neuroscience and Brain-like AI",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in Computational Neuroscience and Brain-like AI Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in Computational Neuroscience and Brain-like AI KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Job description The objective of the research is to develop brain plausible neural network models of brain’s cognitive and perceptual capabilities. In particular, you are expected to build and study cortex-inspired feed-forward and recurrent networks within the context of semi-supervised and unsupervised pattern recognition problems as well as decision making tasks. Your duties will include reviewing relevant literature, designing and simulating neural network models, analyzing and interpreting results, and benchmarking brain-inspired architectures against conventional machine learning methods. You are also expected to actively participate in academic discussions with supervisors at KTH and to write scientific papers. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. As an applicant you should have good programming skills not only in Python but also C++ and capability to develop scalable code to be deployed on supercomputers. You should also have fundamental knowledge in computational neuroscience and machine learning, neural netaorks in particular. It is necessary that you are aware and well informed about diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality. As an applicant you should have experience publishing academic work, as well as strong English language skills and good oral and written communication abilities, since this is required in the daily work. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline. We prefer you have prior experience in developing and simulating both spiking and non-spiking neural networks with local learning rules. It is commendable if you have good collaborative skills and can demonstrate examples of your independence in research. It is also appreciated if you also have some pedagogical experience. Knowledge of and skills in MPI and GPU programming, along with experience running large-scale computational simulations, are desirable qualifications. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, three years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3435 Published 09.Oct.2026 Last application date 18.Oct.2026 Contact Pawel Herman paherman@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/972326?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Large Language Model inferencing",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in Large Language Model inferencing Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in Large Language Model inferencing KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Job description The advertised post-doctoral position is within an ambitious, 5-year Wallenberg Scholar project titled \"Scalable and adaptive inferencing for democratizing AI\". In this 18 Million SEK project, we want to dramatically reduce the cost and power for serving large language models such as ChatGPT. More project information and our project page with early publications. The work will primarily entail design, implementation, and evaluation of distributed systems and networks for machine learning inference. Applying machine learning concepts, with the goal of devising agentic frameworks, will also be a part of the project. As a member of the research lab, you will be involved in experimental systems work in collaboration with faculty members and several doctoral students at our research lab. You will contribute to scientific publications as well as to new grant applications. The work will be in collaboration with Professor Dejan Kostic and Associate Professor Marco Chiesa. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. You should also have a solid background in distributed systems, networking, programming and operating systems, and very good knowledge of English in speech and writing as it is required in day to day work. It is important that you have very good skills in critical thinking and very good knowledge of C++, Python, Linux, and some scripting language. We are seeking a highly motivated candidate with a willingness to experiment and explore, with international publications in journals and top conferences. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Teaching abilities and awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality. You are a good collaborator but can also work independently. Experience with machine learning, GPU programming, or large-scale inference systems. Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3247 Published 23.Sep.2026 Last application date 21.Oct.2026 Contact Dejan Kostic dmk@kth.se Marco Chiesa mchiesa@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
