    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/974287?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in sustainable generative artificial intelligence for media",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in sustainable generative artificial intelligence for media Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in sustainable generative artificial intelligence for media KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Job description The five-year research project FrugalAI is exploring the impacts of using generative artificial intelligence (GenAI) for the creation of media content. Current genAI models, used for generating music, images, text, and other media, rely on vast data sets and require significant computational resources. Training genAI models and employing them on a global scale contributes to substantial energy consumption, resource depletion, and increased carbon emissions, exacerbating environmental harm. Our project aims to develop and promote an innovative, sustainable alternative to existing large and commercial genAI systems. It aims to reduce the environmental footprint of genAI technologies while fostering positive social impacts by prioritizing small, ethically sourced data sets, local models and compute, and encouraging sustainable behavior among users. The research and development conducted in the project can be regarded as situated within the area of human-centered AI. FrugalAI has the following objectives: Estimate the environmental impact of current big-data genAI. Construct a set of open-source frugal genAI tools based on small, ethical data. Map the impact on social sustainability that emerges from using frugal genAI. Compare the environmental impact of these tools with big-data genAI tools. Propose and apply evaluation metrics that consider resource use. Investigate implications for other genAI applications (e.g., image generation). The postdoctoral researcher, having a background related to HCI and machine learning, will contribute to all objectives over a period of two years at 100% time. Working with a diverse team of engineers, musicologists, and designers, the job will include the following tasks: Contribute to the development of an interactive online broadcasting environment (a prototype is “Stochastic Pirate Radio” KSPR) by designing and maintaining project software, and developing pipelines for creating media programs and the automated monitoring for offensive content, and estimating and tracking energy usage. Research and develop frugal AI principles to reduce model sizes, data, and computation using the state of the art in machine learning. Develop a multi-objective metric of genAI sustainability (environmental, economic, sociocultural), building from C. Douwes, On the Environmental Impact of Deep Generative Models for Audio , Doctoral dissertation, Sorbonne Université 2023). Help organize and run workshops with team members For more information, contact Bob L. T. Sturm ( bobs@kth.se ). Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. The working language of the project is English, so you should have fluency in English. You have a background related to HCI and machine learning As a person you have collaborative abilities Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality It’s commendable if you can work independently Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Cover letter presenting how your background aligns with the tasks of this position, and your interest in the overall project. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3304 Published 01.Oct.2026 Last application date 05.Nov.2026 Contact Bob Sturm bobs@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
