    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/925980?l=en": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Environmental impact analysis",
      "description": "KTH | Associate Professor in Environmental impact analysis Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Associate Professor in Environmental impact analysis School of Architecture and Built Environment at KTH Subject field Environmental impact analysis Subject description The subject environmental impact analysis encompasses theoretical, methodological, and applied research for environmental assessment of projects, plans, and programs. Its core focus is on developing and critically examining how environmental aspects are integrated into planning and decision-making processes to promote sustainable development, with attention to both content and practical application. The subject also includes analysis of how knowledge, methods, and tools are used at various stages of the process, and how these contribute to and influence decision-making, implementation, and follow-up. By employing a range of qualitative and quantitative methods for environmental systems analysis and decision support, the field makes ecological, climate-related, and other sustainability-critical knowledge available for planning purposes. The research is conducted within a context where both Swedish and international perspectives are central. Collaboration with the public sector and the business community is crucial for its relevance and implementation. With an increasing focus on emerging sustainability challenges, such as climate adaptation, digitalization, circular solutions, and equity, the field contributes to the development of future practice, integrated planning processes, and the knowledge required for sustainable urban and regional development. Duties Duties include teaching, course development, and examination at both undergraduate and advanced levels within the subject area and related fields. The associate professor is expected to actively contribute to the development of courses and degree programs at the department and to provide relevant links to society for the student groups involved. It is also crucial that teaching is closely linked to current research to foster a research-integrated educational environment. Teaching, including supervision of degree projects, is conducted in both Swedish and English. Initially, it accounts for approximately 50% of the position but is subject to adjustment based on the department's needs. Administrative and supervisory tasks related to teaching may also be included. Research duties involve conducting independent research within the subject area and actively seeking and securing external research funding. The associate professor is expected to contribute to the department’s development and the academic environment by initiating and participating in research collaborations with other research groups within the department and across KTH. Collaboration with external stakeholders, nationally and internationally, as well as with industry and the public sector, is a vital component in grounding, developing, and realizing the impact of the research. The associate professor is expected to establish and develop independent and internationally recognized research. Duties also include seeking external funding for, and supervising, doctoral students and postdoctoral researchers. The position also entails active participation in academic activities at the department, the school, and KTH, including undertaking positions of trust as well as administrative and leadership roles within the department. The associate professor is also expected to contribute to the department's vision of playing a leading role in achieving KTH's goals regarding sustainable development and climate impact. Eligibility Those eligible to be employed as associate professor are persons who have: 1.    completed a doctorate or possess equivalent scientific expertise or some other professional expertise that is of significance with regard to the subject content of the employment and the duties that are required of the employment, and 2.    demonstrated pedagogical expertise. Assessment criteria The assessment criteria for appointment as an associate professor at KTH shall be the degree of expertise required as a qualification for employment. In addition, the assessment criteria stated in the KTH appointments procedure, section 1.2., apply in relation to the employment profile laid down. Of highest importance is that the applicant has •    scientific expertise in environmental impact analysis •    pedagogical expertise in environmental impact analysis, demonstrated through, among other things, experience of individual supervision at both undergraduate and doctoral levels •    the ability to work within the field in both a Swedish and an international context •    the ability to teach in Swedish Of second highest importance that the applicant has •    the ability to collaborate •    the ability to engage with the surrounding community for mutual exchange and to have worked to ensure that the knowledge and expertise available at the university benefit society It is also important that the applicant has •    expertise in developing and leading activities and staff. For that purpose, the individual is to be knowledgeable about diversity and equal opportunity issues, particularly gender equality. •    administrative expertise Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives can be found at KTH's webpage . Application Your application should follow KTH's CV template for employment of teachers . It is the responsibility of the applicant to ensure that the application is complete according to the requirements in the ad and CV template. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply to this position online. For more information regarding KTH's assessement, see Appointments procedure at the Royal Institute of Technology Other For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process please read here. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. Guidance on relocating and settling in at KTH and in Sweden. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly pay Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2126 Published 02.Oct.2026 Last application date 10.Nov.2026 Contact Anna Björklund annab@kth.se Maria Malmström malmstro@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/981310?l=en": {
      "title": "Research Engineer in development of brain-inspired artificial intelligence",
      "description": "KTH | Research Engineer in development of brain-inspired artificial intelligence kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Research Engineer in development of brain-inspired artificial intelligence KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Job description The goal of this work is to develop brain-like network architectures and carry out high-performance, large-scale implementations. Your responsibilities will include studying relevant literature, designing and simulating large-scale neural network models on various hardware platforms, including neuromorphic hardware. You will also be expected to actively participate in academic discussions with advisors at KTH and to write scientific articles. Qualifications Requirements Applicants must have obtained a graduate degree at advanced level (higher education) in Computer Science or a related field. As an applicant, you should have strong programming skills and the ability to develop scalable code for running on supercomputers. You should also have a deep understanding of artificial intelligence and machine learning, particularly regarding neural networks. It is essential that you are knowledgeable and well-informed about issues related to diversity and equal opportunity, with a particular focus on gender equality. Applicants must have a good command of English and strong verbal and written communication skills, since this is required in the daily work. You have strong collaborative skills and can also demonstrate independence in research and development. As an applicant, you are expected to build cortex-inspired neural networks for problems in semi-supervised and unsupervised learning. Your primary responsibilities will involve implementation and optimization on various hardware platforms, including neuromorphic hardware. Preferred qualifications We would prefer that you have prior experience developing and simulating large-scale brain-like neural networks with local learning rules. Knowledge of and proficiency in GPU programming, as well as experience running large-scale computational simulations, are desirable qualifications. Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to12 months part-time, with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Part-time Full-time equivalent 50% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3617 Published 21.Oct.2026 Last application date 30.Oct.2026 Contact Pawel Herman paherman@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/981782?l=en": {
      "title": "Research Student Assistant in Traffic Video Anomaly Understanding",
      "description": "KTH | Research Student Assistant in Traffic Video Anomaly Understanding Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Research Student Assistant in Traffic Video Anomaly Understanding KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Architecture and Built Environment Job description We are seeking a research student assistant interested in computer vision, video understanding and multimodal artificial intelligence. The project addresses abnormal, risky and assistance-requiring events involving vulnerable individuals, including people with disabilities, in traffic-related environments. The assistant will help prepare traffic accident and fall-related video datasets, collect and annotate publicly available videos, and develop event labels for temporal boundaries, spatial locations, causes and severity. Tasks also include preparing question–answer data, supporting the post-training and evaluation of a vision–language model, assessing event detection and spatiotemporal localization, and documenting experiments and research results. Qualifications Requirements You should be admitted to first or second-level cycle education at a  Swedish university Preferred qualifications Student at KTH Knowledge of Python, machine learning and computer vision; experience in video processing, dataset preparation or annotation is an advantage. Experience with vision–language models, PyTorch, model fine-tuning, video anomaly detection or evaluation of AI systems is an advantage. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . Application Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application should include the following documents: CV Transcript records Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 3 months, with access according to agreement. Others For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Part-time Full-time equivalent 50% First day of employment 1 November 2026 – 31 January 2027 Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3628 Published 21.Oct.2026 Last application date 30.Oct.2026 Contact Yancheng Ling yancheng@kth.se Zhenliang Ma zhema@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
