    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/955894?l=en": {
      "title": "Undergraduate assistant - Support hardware startups",
      "description": "KTH | Undergraduate assistant - Support hardware startups at KTH Innovation! Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Undergraduate assistant - Support hardware startups at KTH Innovation! KTH Royal Institute of Technology, Support services at KTH Technical Student for KTH Innovation Makerspace – Help Startups Go from Idea to Prototype! KTH Innovation is one of Europe’s leading startup hubs. Each year, we help hundreds of students and researchers explore ideas and launch startups. Our alumni include Blykalla, Airmee, TERASi, SuperAnnotate and Flox, as well as founders behind ventures such as Lovable and Neko Health. An important part of our work is supporting teams developing physical products. That’s where you come in! Your Role We are looking for a student with an interest in, and experience from design and product development who wants a flexible part-time job alongside their studies. You will apply your technical skills, develop your prototyping expertise and gain insight into how startups and early-stage technologies evolve. As a student assistant, you will support teams developing physical products, helping them move from ideas to functional prototypes in the KTH Innovation Makerspace. Your responsibilities include: Providing hands-on and digital support with CAD, 3D printing, laser cutting, basic electronics and prototype fabrication. You will particularly help others use 3D printers effectively and safely. Guiding teams in defining what to test, choosing prototyping methods, planning iterations and evaluating results. Teams remain responsible for their own product development. Introducing teams to the makerspace, its tools and equipment, and helping maintain welcoming, well-organized routines and workflows. You will also contribute to events, study visits and administrative tasks. You will join the KTH Innovation student assistant team and collaborate with KTH's central makerspace, other makerspaces at KTH and student associations working with hardware. The position is 30%, with flexible working hours to accommodate your studies. Some evening events are included. Read more about KTH Innovation Qualifications Required - what is actually needed in the role Admission to a first-, second- or third-cycle programme at a Swedish university. Good spoken and written English as it is needed in daily work. Practical knowledge of CAD software. Experience using 3D printers. Personal Attributes We value inclusion, openness and diversity. You should enjoy helping people with different backgrounds and levels of experience feel welcome and confident in exploring their ideas. You enjoy collaborating with and helping others. You are solution-oriented and can troubleshoot practical technical problems independently. You communicate technical concepts clearly and adapt your guidance to different levels of knowledge. You take responsibility, show initiative and work independently. You contribute to a welcoming environment where everyone feels comfortable asking questions, experimenting and learning. Meriting- desirable, but not all are expected At least one year of studies remaining at KTH. Experience in physical product prototyping and product development. Practical experience building hardware and/or software solutions. Experience with makerspace equipment and manufacturing methods, such as laser cutting, casting, vacuum forming or 3D scanning. Experience from student associations or other organizations connected to hardware and/or startups. Knowledge of electronics. Swedish language skills as it fascilitates daily work. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Trade union representatives Contact details for trade union representatives . Application Apply through KTH’s recruitment system. As an applicant, you are responsible for making sure your application is complete when submitted. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the final day of the application period. Instructions The application must include the following documents: A cover letter (maximum one page) in which you briefly: Explain why you are interested in innovation, prototyping, and the startup environment. Provide a concrete example of something you have built, developed, or prototyped, and describe the tools, methods, or techniques you used. Provide a concrete example of a time you helped someone else solve a technical problem, learn a tool, or make progress on a project. A short CV (maximum one page) that focuses on the requirements and the additional desirable qualifications. Applications that do not follow these instructions may be assessed less favourably. Your application must be received by KTH no later than midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time) on the final application date. About the position The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to one year with a possibility for extension, with a starting date to be agreed upon. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment . It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence KTH as a workplace Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Part-time Full-time equivalent 30% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2656 Published 30.Oct.2026 Last application date 15.Nov.2026 Contact Lisa Ericsson 08-7906607 lisaeric@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/984656?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in techno-economic analysis of resilient urban energy systems",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoctoral position in techno-economic analysis of resilient urban energy systems Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoctoral position in techno-economic analysis of resilient urban energy systems KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Do you want to develop and evaluate concepts for how a brand-new urban district can be supplied with both heat and electricity robustly, even when something unexpected happens, and see your analyses used as decision support by the municipality that will build it? Welcome with your application. The position is part of a collaboration between KTH, Uppsala University and Uppsala Municipality on the energy system in Uppsala’s south-eastern districts. This is one of Sweden’s largest urban development projects, with 21,500 homes planned by 2050. You will work on a real question in a live setting, where your results directly affect how a district is built. Two postdocs are being recruited in parallel to work closely together: one at KTH (this position) and one at Uppsala University. Part of the working time is spent at Uppsala Municipality , which gives direct access to planning documentation, stakeholders and the questions that are current during implementation. The project is part of the research area STandUP for Energy. Job description The position aims to generate and evaluate concepts for the energy supply of Uppsala’s south-eastern districts, and to analyse them techno-economically as decision support for the municipality. Duties include: developing, modelling and comparing concepts for a flexible low-temperature heating system techno-economically evaluating a flexible electricity microgrid analysing the heating system and the electricity microgrid as an integrated multi-energy system quantifying the socio-economic value of the energy system’s resilience analysing the security of supply of the heat and electricity systems during disruptions, and how concept and sizing choices affect recovery time and outage costs developing scenarios for the district’s build-out, connection rates, energy demand, technology rollout and system configuration carrying out techno-economic analyses of the integrated system analysing business models and implementation models for both systems translating the results into decision support publishing results in scientific journals and presenting them at conferences taking part in applications for external research funding, nationally and within the EU Qualifications Requirements A PhD in energy technology, energy systems, mechanical engineering or equivalent, or a foreign degree deemed equivalent. The degree must be completed no later than when the employment decision is made. Documented experience of modelling, optimization and analysis of energy systems, preferably integrated or multi-energy systems Experience of techno-economic analysis, investment planning, infrastructure sizing or operational optimization Knowledge of thermal energy systems, for example district heating, heat pumps or thermal storage Understanding of energy markets and policy instruments, for both heat and electricity Programming skills and experience developing or applying computational models for energy system analysis The ability to express yourself in English, orally and in writing, as English is used daily in the project Personal skills Good collaboration skills and the ability to communicate research results to stakeholders outside academia Goal-oriented and self-driven approach to work Preferred qualification A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Experience in low-temperature heating systems, waste heat recovery, thermal storage or other distributed energy resources Experience in modelling, optimization or sector coupling of integrated energy systems Experience in resilience or reliability analysis of energy systems, security of supply, or valuation of outage costs Experience in energy economics/business models, or collaboration with municipalities, authorities or industry Commitment to and awareness of gender equality, diversity, and equal opportunities. knowledge of Swedish, or willingness to learn it, for the work with the municipality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3737 Published 30.Oct.2026 Last application date 27.Nov.2026 Contact Björn Laumert laumert@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/984227?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in agentic AI for spatial biology of the human gut",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in agentic AI for spatial biology of the human gut Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in agentic AI for spatial biology of the human gut KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health Job description How do cells organize into complex human tissues and can AI uncover tissue architecture in health and disease? The Koplev lab at KTH Royal Institute of Technology and SciLifeLab is recruiting an ambitious postdoctoral researcher to lead the development of computational methods, modelling human tissue architecture using single-cell and spatial transcriptomics data. The position is part of a research project funded by Digital Futures in collaboration with Assistant Professor Wei Ouyang's AICell Lab. The project aims to develop autonomous AI scientist systems that perfor end-to-end bioinformatics analysis, including writing and executing code, evaluating results, refining analytical approaches, and generating testable biological hypotheses. A central challenge is establishing how AI agents can be rigorously tested and supervised to enable scientific discovery. The research will focus on human gastrointestinal diseases, including Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis, and colorectal cancer. The project will develop and evaluate machine learning approaches for identifying cell types, characterizing tissue niches across disease states. The successful candidate will lead computational research projects at the intersection of artificial intelligence, machine learning, and spatial biology. Responsibilities include: Developing and evaluating AI agents for automated analysis of single-cell and spatial transcriptomics data. Integrating large-scale spatial transcriptomics datasets across technologies, tissues, and diseases. Investigating biological mechanisms of tissue organization, including immune cell migration and intercellular signalling. Disseminating research findings through scientific publications, conferences, and open-source software. The successful candidate will join a growing and collaborative research group at the Department of Gene Technology and SciLifeLab. The lab's broader research programme investigates tissue architecture across the gastrointestinal tract, heart, and cardiovascular system, providing opportunities to develop new scientific directions according to the candidate's interests and expertise. The postdoctoral researcher will contribute to the scientific development of the group, including mentoring students and supporting collaborative projects. The position offers opportunities to develop scientific leadership skills and establish an independent research profile in preparation for a future career as a group leader or senior research scientist. More information: https://www.scilifelab.se/researchers/simon-koplev/ Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. Substantial research expertise in computational biology methods for single-cell or spatial transcriptomics data. Proven scientific excellence as evidenced by strong scientific publications and track record relative to career stage. Experience developing or applying machine learning methods, including deep learning, foundation models, large language models, or autonomous AI agents. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline. Highly creative researcher with broad scientific curiosity Mastery of data visualization and scientific communication Exceptional collaborative abilities Self-motivated individual with ability to work independently Teaching and mentorship abilities or interests in personal development Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality We welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds and with complementary strengths. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Brief letter of motivation describing why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max two pages. Copy of diploma from your PhD. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3723 Published 30.Oct.2026 Last application date 29.Nov.2026 Contact Simon Koplev koplev@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/983207?l=en": {
      "title": "Researcher in development of brain-inspired artificial intelligence",
      "description": "KTH | Researcher in development of brain-inspired artificial intelligence Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Researcher in development of brain-inspired artificial intelligence KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Job description As an applicant, you are expected to build cortex-inspired neural networks for problems in semi-supervised and unsupervised learning. Your primary responsibilities will involve implementation and optimization on various hardware platforms, including neuromorphic hardware. The goal of this work is to develop brain-like network architectures and carry out high-performance, large-scale implementations. Your responsibilities will include studying relevant literature, designing and simulating large-scale neural network models on various hardware platforms, including neuromorphic hardware. You will also be expected to actively participate in academic discussions with advisors at KTH and to write scientific articles. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree at advanced level (higher education) in Computer Science or a related field. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. As an applicant, you should have strong programming skills and the ability to develop scalable code for running on supercomputers. You should also have a deep understanding of artificial intelligence and machine learning, particularly regarding neural networks. It is essential that you are knowledgeable and well-informed about issues related to diversity and equal opportunity, with a particular focus on gender equality. Applicants must have a good command of English and strong verbal and written communication skills, since this is required in the daily work. Preferred qualifications We would prefer that you have prior experience developing and simulating large-scale brain-like neural networks with local learning rules. It is advantageous if you have strong collaborative skills and can also demonstrate independence in research and development. Knowledge of and proficiency in GPU programming, as well as experience running large-scale computational simulations, are desirable qualifications. Furthermore, we would prefer that you have teaching ability and prior experience of developing and leading activities and staff. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH . Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max two pages long. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 6 months, with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3663 Published 03.Nov.2026 Last application date 12.Nov.2026 Contact Pawel Herman paherman@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/981104?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in hormone sensing between biophysics and biotechnology",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student in hormone sensing between biophysics and biotechnology kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student in hormone sensing between biophysics and biotechnology KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Project description Third-cycle subject: Applied Physics or Biotechnology Hormones shape metabolism, fertility, mood and sleep, yet they are rarely measured, and then mostly by blood tests in a clinic. In the Hormones Project, funded by KTH InspireLab, we are developing an affordable optical system that measures six hormones in urine, at home, every day. As a doctoral student you will work at the border between biophysics and biotechnology: you will prepare and characterise urine samples, validate against established laboratory methods, and design and test the detection system. The project is jointly led by three research leaders at AlbaNova and SciLifeLab. Read more about the project here Supervision: Carlota Canalias, Michael Fokine and Cecilia Williams are proposed to supervise the doctoral student. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge The candidate must have a master's degree in biophysics, biotechnology, biomedicine, physics or a closely related field. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach, analyze and work with complex issues, demonstrate knowledge of gender equality from an intersectional perspective and an understanding of why gender aspects are important when conducting research and developing technology, demonstrate good written and spoken English, as it is required in day to day work. experience of laboratory work with optical, spectroscopic, biophysical or bioanalytical methods is considered a merit. Experience of working in multidisciplinary teams is also a merit. Furthermore, the candidate should have a genuine interest in learning new disciplines. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages. Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. A statement (maximum 1 page) on your view of and vision for gender equality and technology. A copy of your master's thesis or similar. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3677 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 19.Nov.2026 Contact Carlota Canalias Gomez ccg@kth.se Michael Fokine fokine@kth.se Cecilia Williams cwil@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/980203?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral (Licentiate) in wastewater technology",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral (Licentiate) in wastewater technology kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral (Licentiate) in wastewater technology KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Architecture and Built Environment Project description Third-cycle subject: Water and environmental technology The Water and Environmental Engineering (WEE) research group at the Department of Sustainable Development, Environmental Science and Engineering (SEED), KTH Royal Institute of Technology, is seeking two motivated applicants to work on innovative solutions for wastewater and sludge management. Our group conducts research in a broad range of areas, including water quality, micropollutants, resource recovery, and sustainable treatment technologies. This project focuses on understanding the fate and behavior of PFAS during wastewater treatment and developing innovative technologies for PFAS removal and destruction. The work includes the analysis of wastewater, PFAS and their transformation products in wastewater, the evaluation of PFAS adsorption technologies using biochar and GAC, and the investigation of electrochemical processes for PFAS transformation Supervision: Associate professor Sahar Dalahmeh is proposed to supervise the doctoral student. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge The applicant must have a master’s degree in Environmental Science, Environmental Engineering, Chemical Engineering, Chemistry, or a related field. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach, analyze and work with complex issues, present background in analytical methods (e.g., LC-MS and spectrophotometry) demonstrate experience or interest in wastewater treatment and laboratory analysis of wastewater and sludge and, demonstrate experience with practical hands-on work with wastewater treatment processes at large-scale wastewater treatment plants. Knowledge of programming and data analysis (e.g., Python, R, or MATLAB) is considered an advantage. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Licentiate degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages. Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3548 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 25.Nov.2026 Contact Sahar Dalahmeh dalahmeh@kth.se Maria Malmström maria.malmstrom@abe.kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/985107?l=en": {
      "title": "Researcher in Privacy-Preserving AI",
      "description": "KTH | Researcher in Privacy-Preserving AI Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Researcher in Privacy-Preserving AI KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Job description The AICell Lab ( https://aicell.io ) in the department of Applied Physics at KTH and Science for Life Laboratory is a new research group funded by the Data-driven Life Science Fellows program. The group, led by Wei Ouyang, focuses on building AI systems for data-driven cell and molecular biology. To expand the team, we are now opening a position for a researcher in privacy-preserving AI for sensitive biomedical data. The researcher will play a key role in developing our platform where AI agents analyse data where it is, so that sensitive data never has to leave the data owner’s environment. This is a unique opportunity to help shape how sensitive data can be shared and used safely in research and healthcare across Europe, and to be part of an enthusiastic and dynamic team. The responsibilities are: Lead research and development of the group’s platform for AI agents and privacy-preserving analysis of sensitive data Represent KTH in EU projects and identify opportunities to use the platform in them Initiate applications for external funding and build collaborations with healthcare, industry and data owners Supervise students and contribute to the supervision of doctoral students in the group Publish research findings in high-quality scientific journals and conferences Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree in a relevant field such as Physics, Computer Science, Bioinformatics, or other life sciences or an equivalent foreign degree. Extensive experience in artificial intelligence, machine learning, and computational biology Collaborative abilities Independence We are looking for someone who is reliable, collaborative, and communicative. You need to be able to work independently, actively contribute to problem solving, and to help move projects forward. It is commendable if you are well organized and thorough. As an employee at KTH, awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality, is required. Preferred qualifications International postdoctoral experience Training in machine learning, information security or data protection Experience of advanced use of AI agents and workflows built on large language models, e.g. multi-agent systems Experience of EU-funded projects and of working with European research infrastructures Experience in a management or leadership role, e.g. head of a unit or platform in academia, a research infrastructure or other R&D work, with responsibility for operations, budget and external collaborations A record of winning external research or innovation funding in open competition, e.g. a personal research grant or fellowship from a national or international funder Knowledge of regulations for sensitive data, e.g. GDPR and the European Health Data Space (EHDS) Scientific publications in the field Good knowledge of Swedish as is required for the day-to day work. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH . Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience, knowledge and representative publications. Please also provide your Github/Gitlab/Bitbucket etc. handle if possible. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Personal letter about your previous experience, personal competencies, career goals, why you want to conduct research, your interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max two pages long. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 12 months (or years), with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3753 Published 06.Nov.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Wei Ouyang weio@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/987134?l=en": {
      "title": "Research student assistant in Nanoparticle/Polymer Composites for Photovoltaics",
      "description": "KTH | Research student assistant in Nanoparticle/Polymer Composites for Photovoltaics Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Research student assistant in Nanoparticle/Polymer Composites for Photovoltaics KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Job description A new modern direction in photovoltaics is building-integration, where functional components become an intrinsic part of the construction materials. Typically, a “Building Integrated Photovoltaics” system (BIPV) consists of integrated PV modules into the building envelope, such as the roof or the facade. This concept can be also extended to windows. Although the inherent window transparency should be maintained, even a partial conversion of the sunlight to electrical energy can generate sizeable power quantities where large surface areas are involved. In this project luminescent solar concentrators (“Quantum Dot Glass”) based on nanocomposite films, laminated on glass, will be investigated for this purpose. Silicon quantum dots, metal nanocrlusters, transition metal-doped nanoparticles, silicon nanospheres, etc. will be considered as fluorophores and off-stoichiometry thiol-enes as a primary host polymer. The work will consist of nanoparticle synthesis, their surface functionalization, preparation of a polymer/nanoparticle hybrid material, device assembly and its characterization. Nano-characterization and optical measurement facilities in our Albano Laboratory will be extensively used to study synthesized materials and devices. The work is a part of a European project with academia and industry on smart windows, and a close following on deadlines for milestones and deliverables is important. Qualifications Requirements You should be admitted to first or second-level cycle education at a Swedish university A relevant education background, such as Nanotechnology Program Chemistry Track. The candidate is supposed to have adequate knowledge of nanoparticle chemical synthesis and characterization techniques, optical phenomena in materials, and photovoltaic device operation. Preferred qualifications Student at KTH Very good grades i Master level courses Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . Application Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application should include the following documents: CV Transcript records Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 6 months, with access according to agreement. Others For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Part-time Full-time equivalent 25% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3813 Published 06.Nov.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Ilja Sytjugov ilyas@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/979760?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student on calculations of flow through hydro dam bottom outlets",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student on calculations of flow through hydro dam bottom outlets kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student on calculations of flow through hydro dam bottom outlets KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Architecture and Built Environment Project description Third-cycle subject: Civil and Architectural Engineering The division for Concrete Structures at KTH Civil and Architectural Engineering is in search for a doctoral student to be assigned a project on hydraulic design of structures within hydropower. Many dam facilities have been rebuilt or are to be upgraded to achieve a higher level of safety. A bottom outlet is a critical structure from both a dam safety and operational point of view. Emergency lowering of a reservoir's water level is entirely dependent on it and the outlet can also be used in the event of a spillway overflow. To ensure safe operation and long service life, it is necessary to understand the mechanisms and take appropriate measures. The project is part of a national research program within the hydropower area called SVC – Swedish Centre for Sustainable Hydropower. The research is carried out together with senior researchers at KTH and in interdisciplinary research collaboration with international researchers and industry partners. The aim is to understand the behaviour of the bottom discharge with respect to air entrainment through physical and numerical modelling and to help propose cost-effective measures to maintain its normal function. Supervision: The doctoral student is proposed to be supervised by Professor Anders Ansell, Assistant professor Shicheng Li and PhD James Yang. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach and analyze and work with complex issues. The ideal candidate has an exam that covers the areas of hydraulics, concrete structures and structural mechanics, also with experiences from hydraulic model tests, and from using CFD and/or FEM software for advanced analysis. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages.Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment 2027-01-01, or according to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3532 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Anders Ansell anders.ansell@byv.kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/979786?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student on structural rehabilitation of concrete hydro dams",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student on structural rehabilitation of concrete hydro dams kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student on structural rehabilitation of concrete hydro dams KTH, School of Architecture and Built Environment Project description Third-cycle subject: Civil and Architectural Engineering The division for Concrete Structures at KTH Civil and Architectural Engineering is in search for a doctoral student to be assigned a project on reinforced concrete structures within hydropower. Dams in Sweden and many other countries are aging and have an average age of over 50 years. Spillways and associated concrete structures play a crucial role in reducing the risk of dam overflow and serious damage. However, over the years, these have been exposed to varying flows, including extreme high flows, which in many cases has caused damage. The most common repair method today is underwater concrete casting, which is costly and experience shows that many such repairs do not last as long as planned. The project is part of a national research program within the hydropower area called SVC – Swedish Centre for Sustainable Hydropower. The research is carried out together with senior researchers at KTH and in interdisciplinary research collaboration with international researchers and industry partners. The aim is to create a better understanding of how damage occurs, what forces and hydraulic loads act, and how these affect both concrete and the rock subsurface. The project is expected to provide decision-making information for maintenance, repair and reconstruction of embankments and associated structures. Supervision: The doctoral student is proposed to be supervised by Professor Anders Ansell, Docent Andreas Sjölander and PhD Erik Nordström. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach and analyze and work with complex issues. The ideal candidate has an exam that covers the areas of concrete structures, structural engineering and structural mechanics, also with experiences from structural dynamic analysis and testing, and from using advanced finite element modelling for structural analysis. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages.Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment 2027-01-01, or according to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3533 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Anders Ansell anders.ansell@byv.kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
