    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/980433?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student on structural health monitoring of concrete hydro dams",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student on structural health monitoring of concrete hydro dams kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student on structural health monitoring of concrete hydro dams KTH, School of Architecture and Built Environment Project description Third-cycle subject: Civil and Architectural Engineering The division for Concrete Structures at KTH Civil and Architectural Engineering is in search for a doctoral student to be assigned a project on reinforced concrete structures within hydropower. Dams in Sweden and many other countries are aging and have an average age of over 50 years. As they age, damage becomes more common. Typical visible damage includes cracks, leaching and scratching of the concrete surface and can be detected by visual inspections. However, there are also many other types of damage that may be more difficult to detect, such as reinforcement corrosion. In order to maintain older dams in full operation with a high level of safety, the response of the dams should be continuously monitored. The project is part of a national research program within the hydropower area called SVC – Swedish Centre for Sustainable Hydropower. The research is carried out together with senior researchers at KTH and in interdisciplinary research collaboration with international researchers and industry partners. The aim is to create a good understanding of the structural response of concrete dams during normal operation, what should be measured and where sensors should be placed. The project will also identify which types of sensors are appropriate to use and identify reasonable alarm limits. Supervision: The doctoral student is proposed to be supervised by Docent Andreas Sjölander, Professor Anders Ansell and PhD Erik Nordström. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach and analyze and work with complex issues. The ideal candidate has an exam that covers the areas of concrete structures, structural engineering and structural mechanics, also with experiences from structural dynamic analysis and testing, and from using advanced finite element modelling for structural analysis. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages.Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment 2027-01-01, or according to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3554 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Anders Ansell ansell@kth.se Annika Gram agram@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/981025?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student (Licentiate) in evaluation and policy for nature-based solutions",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student (Licentiate) in evaluation and policy for nature-based solutions kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student (Licentiate) in evaluation and policy for nature-based solutions KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Architecture and Built Environment Project description Third-cycle subject: Sustainability studies We are seeking applicants with an interest in wetland restoration as a nature-based solution for sustainable water supply under changing climate conditions. The  will combine methods such as policy analysis, value mapping, socio-economic analysis, and qualitative research methods. The overall aim is to develop policy and valuation frameworks that link wetland indicators to societal benefits and costs, as well as to practical policy instruments and financing mechanisms. The successful applicant will primarily contribute to: (1) developing policy-relevant indicators for the water-related benefits of restored wetlands and exploring how these can be translated into information relevant for valuation, decision-making, and policy development; and (2) analyzing and mapping the values generated by wetland restoration for different stakeholders and society as a whole, including benefits, costs, and risks, as well as how these are distributed among different actors. The work will be carried out in close collaboration with researchers and societal stakeholders in two interdisciplinary research projects. The position is based at the Department of Sustainable Development, Environmental Science and Engineering (SEED). Supervision: Zahra Kalantari is proposed to supervise. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge Professional working proficiency in Swedish is a requirement, as this will be required in day-to-day work In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach, analyze and work with complex issues, present strong written and oral communication skills, particularly in communicating research findings. present knowledge of environmental or sustainability policy, environmental economics, socio-economic analysis, sustainability governance, or a related field; present knowledge and experience in cost-benefit analysis, policy analysis, or the analysis of policy instruments, It is considered an advantage if you have: experience with qualitative and/or quantitative social science research methods, an interest in nature-based solutions, ecosystem services, water-related issues, or climate adaptation and experience of working with stakeholders outside academia After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Licentiate degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages. Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3577 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Sofia Lingegård sofilin@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/984498?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in Wearable Biofeedback Systems for Cardiovascular Health",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student in Wearable Biofeedback Systems for Cardiovascular Health kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student in Wearable Biofeedback Systems for Cardiovascular Health KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health Project description Third-cycle subject: Technology and Health We are looking for an inquisitive person to pursue a PhD in Wearable Biofeedback Systems for Cardiovascular Health in the Department of Biomedical Engineering and Health Systems. The ideal candidate has a background in biomedical, electrical, mechanical engineering or computer/data science. You will be an integral part of the growing Intelligent Heart Technology Lab , whose mission is to advance cardiovascular health technologies. We develop and research implantable and wearable systems, including artificial hearts, blood pressure sensors, and soft robots for the heart, which adapt to people's physiological and mental needs. In this project, you will closely collaborate with clinicians (Karolinska Institute), enabling interdisciplinary discourse for maximal innovative breakthroughs. The doctoral student will lead research into the physical mechanisms underlying the beneficial physiological effects of cardiac locomotor coupling. The project will combine advanced signal processing, physics-informed data science, embedded systems, and modelling of cardiovascular physiology. The doctoral student will also be responsible to validate the technologies developed in human-subject studies. Supervision: Associate Professor Seraina Dual, KTH and Associate Professor Eric Rullman Karolinska Institute Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach, analyze and work with complex issues, strive for high-quality research, demonstrate research interests in bio-signal processing, system modeling, embedded systems, and physiology. apply their relevant technical expertise, contribute to a caring, inclusive, and enjoyable work environment, engage in interdisciplinary research with the aim of achieving real-world impact and apply technical expertise in medical technology, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering, robotics or computer/data science. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages. Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3731 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Seraina Anne Dual seraina@kth.se Aurora Rosato rosato@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/987236?l=en": {
      "title": "Researcher in ionic materials for supercapacitors",
      "description": "KTH | Researcher in ionic materials for supercapacitors Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Researcher in ionic materials for supercapacitors KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health Job description The driver is the neeed for material science to provide sustainable solutons in energy production. The position is concerned with research into the design of a novel supercapacitor based on the self-assembly of ionic materials at interfaces. It will span research from understanding properties of ionic liquids and their solutions, the role of structure and charge, and the response to surface potential. The succesful applicant will be responsible for driving a proof of concept project, performing the necessary experiments, interpreting them and writing reports and scientific publications in high ranked journals. The job will also entail coordinating input from a multidisciplinary team and designing a supercapacitor demonstrator. The School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health CBH conducts research and education in areas that cover several global challenges. Among them are the need of sustainable energy, health and aging population, climate change, sustainable production and working life, food production and clean water. It consists of 9 units, amongst which The Chemistry Department is one of the largest. Research and teaching are very diverse but are united by a molecular approach. We work on important research problems with broad relevance for energy, materials, environment and health, and a common theme is materials and molecules at interfaces. Surface and Corrosion Science is one of 4 divisions within the department. https://www.kth.se/che/surface and https://www.kth.se/profile/mark/ Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree The research area should be in a relevant discipline, such as surface chemistry, physical chemistry, electrochemistry, materials science, physics or equivalent. Knowledge and experience of advanced level application of at least one relevant experimental technique for the project, such as Atomic force Microscopy, Neutron/Xray reflectometry, surface force measurement, Electrical Impedance Spectroscopy, Interfacial Optical Spectroscopy, Quartz Crystal Microbalance. Fluent written and spoken English as it is required in day to day work. Several years of postdoctoral experience with proven ability to structure and lead beamtimes at large facilities. As a person, you have an enthusiasm for reasearch and for the development, supervision and teaching of your junior colleagues and students. You are independent, self-driven and have a strong collaborative ability, a commitment to benefiting your psychosocial environment and a sense of humour. Your personal convictions are in line with KTHs views on diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Preferred qualifications Experience of research in the ionic liquids field. Prior experience of electrochemical or capacitor systems. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH . Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 1 years, with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment 2027-02-01 or according to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3815 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Mark Rutland mark@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/987716?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in cyber-physical security for smart grids",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in cyber-physical security for smart grids Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in cyber-physical security for smart grids KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Job description As power systems become more digitalised and rely increasingly on synchronised measurements, protecting monitoring data and communications is essential for reliable grid operation. The research will focus on threats such as time-synchronisation attacks and manipulation of monitoring data in wide-area monitoring systems, characterization of their impact on system operation, and their timely detection using machine learning algorithms. The postdoc will develop methods for detection and resilience, and collaborate with an international team to validate them in cyber-physical power-system scenarios. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made Strong publication track record in leading conferences and/or journals in a relevant research field As the work involves international cooperation, excellent skills in English are required, both oral and in writing Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Experience with simulation-based on experimental validation The ability to work in a team as well as independently Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Name and email address of two references. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3828 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 30.Nov.2026 Contact György Dan gyuri@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/978857?l=en": {
      "title": "PhD student in Agentic & Embodied AI for Adaptive Manufacturing Systems",
      "description": "KTH | PhD student in Agentic & Embodied AI for Adaptive Manufacturing Systems kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies PhD student in Agentic & Embodied AI for Adaptive Manufacturing Systems KTH, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Project description Third-cycle subject: Production engineering We are seeking a motivated PhD student to develop AI and robotic methods for adaptive manufacturing systems, with a particular focus on agentic and embodied AI. The research addresses how robots and intelligent production systems can perceive changing conditions, reason about process requirements and constraints, and adapt their actions in real time. The project brings together task level decision intelligence, multimodal perception, digital twin based learning and robot control to enable more flexible and intelligent manufacturing. The research will use battery assembly and disassembly as application scenarios. The PhD student will develop and experimentally validate AI enabled robotic methods in these scenarios, while addressing research questions that are relevant to a broader range of adaptive manufacturing systems. The position is part of a joint PhD program between KTH and Shanghai Jiao Tong University (SJTU). The PhD student will be full time employed at KTH and spend at least 12 months at SJTU, distributed across several research stays. Upon successful completion of the joint PhD programme, KTH and SJTU will jointly issue the PhD degree, with reference to the national accreditation authorized for each university. Supervision: Xi Vincent Wang, Magnus Wiktorsson are proposed to supervise the doctoral student. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach and analyze and work with complex issues. We welcome applicants with backgrounds in robotics, artificial intelligence, computer science, control engineering, automation, production engineering or related fields. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages. Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3497 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 03.Dec.2026 Contact Xi Wang wangxi@kth.se Magnus Wiktorsson magwik@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
