    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/978622?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student (licentiate) in efficient cooling and overheating",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student (licentiate) in efficient cooling and overheating kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student (licentiate) in efficient cooling and overheating KTH, School of Architecture and Built Environment Project description Third-cycle subject: Civil and Architectural Engineering This research project studies energy- and cost-efficient cooling for elderly homes in current and future climates. With KTH, property owners and engineering firms, you will use measurements, calibrated simulations, and techno-economic analysis to assess shading, envelope measures, water-based and borehole-free cooling for climate-resilient design and operation. Supervision: Adnan Ploskic, Sasan Sadrizadeh and Amirmohamad Behzadi are proposed to supervise the doctoral student. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge At least 60 credits at second-cycle level or above in civil and architectural engineering or subjects deemed directly relevant to the specialization. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach, analyze and work with complex issues, present knowledge of building energy, HVAC, thermal comfort or building physics, present knowledge of building simulation (e.g. IDA ICE/TRNSYS/EnergyPlus), coding/data analysis,  (Python/MATLAB), measurement, monitoring or building experiment experience, present knowledge of optimization, techno-economic or statistical knowledge, present strong spoken/written English research experience and present experience from project work with industry or the public sector. The ideal candidate has a master in building technology, services, energy, mechanical or civil engineering, building physics or related fields. The ability to communicate in Swedish, both spoken and written, is considered as strongly meritorious since it is needed during everyday work. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Licentiate degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages. Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3482 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 04.Dec.2026 Contact Adnan Ploskic ploskic@kth.se Amirmohamad Behzadi abehzadi@kth.se Annika Gram agram@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/982870?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in probabilistic machine learning for fluid mechanics",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student in probabilistic machine learning for fluid mechanics kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student in probabilistic machine learning for fluid mechanics KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Project description Third-cycle subject: Engineering Mechanics FLOW is a strong community of researchers engaged in fundamental and applied research in fluid mechanics within the department of Engineering Mechanics. We are currently seeking a PhD student in probabilistic machine learning to join the Fluids and Surfaces Group within FLOW. AI is becoming a critical investment across science and engineering, but fluid mechanics poses particular challenges: flows are often high-dimensional and chaotic, and couple physical processes across many scales. This position offers an exciting opportunity for a highly motivated candidate to develop trustworthy probabilistic methods for inference, optimization and data assimilation. These methods will integrate simulations and experimental data into reliable tools for the design, prediction and control of complex fluid systems. The work focuses on turbulent flows that carry electric charge, as found for example in power transformers. These systems involve coupled processes that are only partly understood, and measurements are sparse and costly. This makes them an ideal testbed, where models must be calibrated, uncertainties quantified and experiments chosen with care, with direct impact on safer and more sustainable power infrastructure. The project is funded by Digital Futures och Hitachi Energy Supervision: Shervin Bagheri and Ozan Öktem are proposed to supervise the student. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach and analyze and work with complex issues. It is meritorious to have experience with fluid mechanics, machine learning and scientific computing, in particular, turbulent flows, Bayesian inference, probabilistic methods and generative AI After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages. Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3646 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 07.Dec.2026 Contact Shervin Bagheri sherwinb@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/985374?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in fusion plasma physics and nuclear engineering",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student in fusion plasma physics and nuclear engineering kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student in fusion plasma physics and nuclear engineering KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Project description Third-cycle subject: Electrical Engineering The provision of plasma-facing components (PFCs) with sufficient lifetime is one of the major technological obstacles to be overcome in developing fusion reactors. Recently, the damage of PFCs due to interaction with runaway electrons (RE) has become a highly critical issue in evaluations of disruption consequences. ITER , currently seeks for the validation of relevant numerical models and tools against existing experimental evidence in order to gain confidence in their applications to predictive reactor modelling. PhD project will focus on the development of modelling tools for simulations of RE-induced PFC damage and their validation against data from EUROfusion Consortium , and DIII-D (USA) . The validated models will be employed for predictive modelling of specific ITER scenarios following input from the ITER Organization. The modelling of MeV RE energy deposition in PFCs will be performed with Monte Carlo simulations. These results will serve as input for the thermomechanical models to be developed in FEM and CFD software to address severe deformation and potential explosion of the material. We offer expertise in the theory and modelling of plasma-surface interactions and electron transport into matter, access to state-of-the-art experimental data from the largest tokamaks worldwide and close collaboration with the Experiments & Plasma Operation Section of the ITER Organization. Supervision: Prof. S. Ratynskaia. Decisions are made on admission. Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge Programming skills in languages such as Fortran, Python, or C/C++,  is required for this position. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work, collaborate with others, have a professional approach, analyze and work with complex issues, demonstrate familiarity with the modelling of electron transport into matter with Monte Carlo techniques (i.e. GEANT4, PENELOPE, FLUKA etc). demonstrate familiarity with basic computational fluid dynamics techniques and demonstrate familiarity with basic computational solid mechanics techniques. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. In the case of studies that are to be completed with a licentiate degree, the total period of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education for two years. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages. Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3761 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 24.Dec.2026 Contact Svetlana Ratynskaia svetlana.ratynskaia@ee.kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
