    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/969098?l=en": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Experimental Astrophysics",
      "description": "KTH | Assistant Professor in Experimental Astrophysics Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Assistant Professor in Experimental Astrophysics KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Subject field Experimental astrophysics. Subject description The subject area is the development of space-based instruments for the detection of ionising radiation from high-energy phenomena, as well as the analysis of observational data from such instruments. Duties The assistant professor shall conduct research within the subject area at a high international level and build up an independent research group. Work duties include establishing a laboratory-based research programme and applying for external research funding. In the long term, the research programme should also include analysis of observational data from the instruments that are developed. The position involves teaching and developing education within the subject area, as well as supervising students and doctoral students. The assistant professor is expected to play a significant role in developing laboratory-based and project-based teaching at the Department of Physics. Some administrative duties are included, and engagement with wider society is expected. The assistant professor should be able to teach in Swedish within four years. If required, a language plan will be drawn up in connection with the appointment. The assistant professor will be given opportunity to develop their independence as researcher and gain accreditation that may allow them to take other teaching positions with higher eligibility requirements (see Chapter 4, Section 12 a of the Swedish Higher Education Ordinance). Following application, the assistant professor can apply for promotion to associate professor in accordance with Chapter 4, Section 12 c of the Higher Education Ordinance. Eligibility An individual who has completed a doctorate or equivalent scientific competence is qualified for appointment as an assistant professor. Candidates who met those qualifications a maximum of seven years before the deadline for applying for the appointment as an assistant professor has expired should be prioritized. Other candidates may also be considered there are special reasons.  Special reasons refers to absence due to illness, parental leave or other similar circumstances. Assessment criteria The assessment criteria for appointment as an assistant professor at KTH are stated in KTH's appointments procedure section 1.3 and apply in relation to the employment profile laid down. Of highest importance is that the applicant has scientific expertise demonstrated through scientific publications, conference presentations, collaborative research projects, and other undertakings in the scientific community such as assignments as a reviewer or expert. the potential to qualify for a higher teaching post. This requires independent development as a researcher and teacher within the subject field, including the ability to establish, renew and develop research activities. an interest in, and understanding of, pedagogical developments within the subject field. Of second highest importance is that the applicant has an interest in, and insight into, leadership in academia, collaboration with wider society, and awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues with a particular focus on gender equality. experience from a postdoctoral visit in a research environment other than the university at which the applicant defended their doctoral thesis. Experience from research and development work within industry or other organizations is considered to correspond to a traditional postdoc visit to another university. It is also important that the applicant has Administrative expertise. Special grounds of assessment for promotion to associate professor When assessing applications for promotion to associate professor, provisions according to Section 1.2.4 of Appointments procedure at KTH will be applied. Ability to teach in Swedish is a merit that is given great importance in the application for promotion. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives can be found at KTH's web page . Application Your application should follow KTH's CV template for employment of teachers . It is the responsibility of the applicant to ensure that the application is complete according to the requirements in the ad and CV template. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Log into KTH recruitment system in order to apply to this position. Other Time limitation:The appointment is for an indefinite term, but no more than six years, and may be extended if, due to the teacher’s absence due to sick leave, parental leave or other special grounds, more time is required to reach the objectives of the appointment. However, the total appointment period may not exceed eight years. The appointment is part of the Tenure Track system at KTH and the assistant professor may apply for promotion to tenured associate professor. For more information regarding KTH's assessment, see Appointments procedure at KTH For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process please read here. Guidance on relocating and settling in at KTH and in Sweden. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Göran Gustafsson (1919–2003) was a successful entrepreneur and philanthropist whose vision was to support research in Sweden by giving young, outstanding researchers the means to develop their research and achieve international success. This assistant professorship is funded by a generous donation from the Göran Gustafsson Foundation. It includes a start-up package that can be used, for example, to set up laboratory-based research or to recruit a postdoc or a PhD student. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly pay Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3097 Published 05.Nov.2026 Last application date 14.Jan.2027 Contact Jonas Strandberg jostran@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/987786?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in AI Agents for Life Science",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in AI Agents for Life Science Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in AI Agents for Life Science KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Job description The AICell Lab (https://aicell.io) in the department of Applied Physics at KTH and Science for Life Laboratory is a research group funded by the Data-driven Life Science Fellows program . The group, led by Wei Ouyang, focuses on building AI systems for data-driven cell and molecular biology. We are seeking a postdoctoral researcher to join our interdisciplinary team and develop innovative AI systems for scientific research and collaboration. The project contributes to a European Union-supported initiative to facilitate access to research infrastructures, particularly within the Euro-BioImaging network, while exploring broader applications of AI agents, collaborative AI systems, and AI-driven scientific discovery in life sciences. You will contribute to the development and evaluation of AI-powered research assistants and multi-agent systems that support scientific workflows, connect researchers with expertise and infrastructure, and facilitate interdisciplinary collaboration. The role combines independent research with project coordination, scientific communication, and close collaboration with researchers, engineers, and European research infrastructure partners. We offer collaboration opportunities with leading research institutions and universities in Europe and the US, learning and thriving in a young and ambitious research group Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. The ability to express yourself in English, as we work in an international environment. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Have a strong interest in scientific research, particularly in life sciences, artificial intelligence, or interdisciplinary research. Have experience or familiarity with scientific data analysis, computational methods, or research workflows in life sciences. Demonstrate interest or experience in AI technologies, including machine learning, large language models, or AI agents for scientific applications. Have strong analytical, conceptual, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to translate complex scientific challenges into practical solutions. Demonstrate excellent communication, organizational, and project management skills, including the ability to coordinate activities and collaborate with diverse stakeholders. Are comfortable working independently and in interdisciplinary, international teams, with a proactive and collaborative approach. Have experience or interest in user-centered design, intuitive user interfaces (UI/UX), interactive applications, or game design, with the ability to create engaging and accessible experiences for scientific users. Have strong teaching abilities. Have awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3836 Published 06.Nov.2026 Last application date 27.Nov.2026 Contact Wei Ouyang weio@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/987657?l=en": {
      "title": "Research student assistent",
      "description": "KTH | Research student assistent kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Research student assistent KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Job description The laboratory at Energy Technology is a collaborative environment where we conduct applied research in thermodynamics, heat transfer, heat storage, fluid machines and heat pumps. Our research projects frequently involve close partnerships with industry partners, creating opportunities to see your work make real-world impact. We maintain a diverse portfolio of both international and national research initiatives led by doctoral students and senior researchers. In this position, you will contribute to research projects focused on heat pumps and heat exchangers. Your responsibilities will include developing innovative design solutions for test rigs, conducting precise measurement assignments, and performing thoughtful data evaluation. You'll have the opportunity to apply your technical expertise while working with a supportive team committed to advancing sustainable energy technologies. We value diverse perspectives and approaches to problem-solving in our collaborative research environment. Qualifications Requirements You should be admitted to first or second-level cycle education at a  Swedish university Preferred qualifications Student at KTH, mechanical engineering masterprogram Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . Application Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application should include the following documents: CV Transcript records Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 12 months, with access according to agreement. Others For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Part-time Full-time equivalent 25% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3827 Published 06.Nov.2026 Last application date 27.Nov.2026 Contact Jens Fridh jens.fridh@energy.kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/987947?l=en": {
      "title": "Researcher in Environmentally Extended Multi-Regional Input-Output Analysis",
      "description": "KTH | Researcher in Environmentally Extended Multi-Regional Input-Output Analysis Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Researcher in Environmentally Extended Multi-Regional Input-Output Analysis KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Architecture and Built Environment Job description The researcher will work with Environmentally Extended Multi-Regional Input-Output Analysis (MRIO) especially focusing on developing and applying methods for prospective studies. The overall aim of the projects is to describe how environmental impacts from consumption can be reduced to sustainable levels. The successful applicant will work in several projects together with researchers and PhD students from KTH, Luxembourg Institute of Science and Technology (LIST) and Statistics Sweden (SCB). The work may include writing applications for further work, presentations at international conferences, interaction with stakeholders, visit to LIST, teaching and supervision of students. The work will be performed at the Division of Sustainability Assessment and Management at the Department of Sustainable Development, Environmental Science and Engineering at KTH, a multidisciplinary department where engineers, and natural and social scientist are working together to understand and develop solutions for a more sustainable society. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree Developed, used and published research on MRIO Preferred qualifications Experience with prospective MRIO Experience with Life Cycle Assessment (LCA), and especially prospective LCA, and other environmental systems analysis tools A background in Industrial Ecology, Economics or Sustainability science Programming skills Experience in teaching The ability to work towards research results being utilized in practice The ability to inform about research and development work Collaborative abilities Independence Experience from writing applications Knowledge in Swedish and Swedish society is useful, since the work will include Swedish case studies and interaction with Swedish stakeholders, but not required Experience of developing and leading activities and staff Knowledge of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH . Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max two pages long. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 12 months, with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3841 Published 09.Nov.2026 Last application date 07.Dec.2026 Contact Göran Finnveden goran.finnveden@abe.kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    }
